// deliberately broken: a define's parameters take no sort. A define is a MACRO —
// its args arrive already elaborated and the body's own elaboration types every
// use of them, so a declared param sort is a second, redundant source of the same
// fact (it can only agree, or spuriously disagree). Write `define isZero(n) = …`.
sort Nat
const ZERO: Nat
define isZero(n: Nat) = n = ZERO
